                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more buttony"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "cbf61199-717d-4dbc-a0c9-65d0fc86ef03",
                        "entry_id": "c63537e7-8600-3361-8dcc-51156f60c3b7",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most buttony"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79ac327b-5e0f-35bb-a431-889cf209d0ef",
                        "entry_id": "c63537e7-8600-3361-8dcc-51156f60c3b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a large number of buttons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f384071-0476-43d3-b019-836a5e378ef4",
                                "sense_id": "79ac327b-5e0f-35bb-a431-889cf209d0ef",
                                "text": "That carriage came round to Gillespie Street every day; that buttony boy sprang up and down from the box with Emmy’s and Jos’s visiting-cards […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f56a848c-2359-4de0-8d59-28bfbe691d6c",
                                "sense_id": "79ac327b-5e0f-35bb-a431-889cf209d0ef",
                                "text": "1869, W. S. Gilbert, “Bob Polter” in Bab Ballads, p. 179,\n“And will my whiskers curl so tight?\nMy cheeks grow smug and muttony?\nMy face become so red and white?\nMy coat so blue and buttony?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31c8cefa-ad5a-4be0-ab4e-96297c011328",
                                "sense_id": "79ac327b-5e0f-35bb-a431-889cf209d0ef",
                                "text": "[…] the inconsistent woman fell upon his buttony breast weeping copiously."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c808901b-bb7d-429e-b31f-40d39fecfcdc",
                                "sense_id": "79ac327b-5e0f-35bb-a431-889cf209d0ef",
                                "text": "That night I lay on a buttony mildewed company mattress between my favorite sheets."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "795dfb8b-6110-36d2-b9cd-2d0715ea1eff",
                        "entry_id": "c63537e7-8600-3361-8dcc-51156f60c3b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a button or buttons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc867f86-da49-4767-8c17-e4fa783369e3",
                                "sense_id": "795dfb8b-6110-36d2-b9cd-2d0715ea1eff",
                                "text": "The Stalactical, is generally of a brassy colour; and so is the blistered buttony Ore, which is protuberant in a semi-circular form […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70bf28a4-f87a-499d-a4e1-632419a1935b",
                                "sense_id": "795dfb8b-6110-36d2-b9cd-2d0715ea1eff",
                                "text": "Tietjens paused and aimed with his hazel stick an immense blow at a tall spike of yellow mullein with its undecided, furry, glaucous leaves and its undecided, buttony, unripe lemon-coloured flowers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8431e118-89c7-4606-a1de-34874a4abc46",
                                "sense_id": "795dfb8b-6110-36d2-b9cd-2d0715ea1eff",
                                "text": "[…] something a little doggish peeped out of the black buttony eyes, a hint of the seraglio."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47d588b9-0188-4c74-ac67-ac522636e84b",
                                "sense_id": "795dfb8b-6110-36d2-b9cd-2d0715ea1eff",
                                "text": "[…] the street had been widened at the expense of a row of sycamores whose blotched bark and buttony seed pods had seemed oddly toylike to him, as if God were an invisible playmate."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2312eb45-fe8e-3975-969d-4dcc0e2aba49",
                        "entry_id": "c63537e7-8600-3361-8dcc-51156f60c3b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a button or buttons.",
                            "Not fully grown and matured; overly small and insufficiently juicy. (of berries)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "40d722cf-54ff-40ba-897c-3bb84a807ba8",
                                "sense_id": "2312eb45-fe8e-3975-969d-4dcc0e2aba49",
                                "text": "But the little dinky, buttony or warty berries must not be packed at all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f61a451-f691-4896-abb2-fb3ac1b79a4a",
                                "sense_id": "2312eb45-fe8e-3975-969d-4dcc0e2aba49",
                                "text": "Some seasons a large number of berries are buttony."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ab956223-2512-3e94-bf70-d38af67e6b24",
                        "entry_id": "c63537e7-8600-3361-8dcc-51156f60c3b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a button or buttons.",
                            "Full-berried. (of hops)"
                        ],
